WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.7 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Whistleblowing, complaints and incident reporting

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Give people safe, visible routes to raise concerns, including about the founders.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Reporting routes give people safe ways to raise concerns about wrongdoing, make complaints and report what happened. In a small founding team, a route to someone outside the founders matters even more.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Three kinds of report

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:40.093
Whistleblowing: Suspected wrongdoing inside: fraud, abuse or cover-ups. It goes to someone independent of those involved. For example: A mentor suspects a founder misused the youth-fund grant and tells the accountant adviser.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:54.015
Complaint: Someone unhappy with your service, product or behaviour. It goes to a named person, with a route beyond. For example: A customer complains about a late cake order; the other founder can review the answer.

7
00:00:54.015 --> 00:01:09.507
Incident: Something that happened: an accident, a data breach or a safeguarding concern. It goes to its owner. For example: A trainee burns a hand on a tray, and the shift lead records it the same day.

8
00:01:09.907 --> 00:01:10.507
Why safe routes matter

9
00:01:10.507 --> 00:01:15.811
1. People must be able to report the founders without fear.

10
00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:20.374
2. Patterns in complaints show you what to improve.

11
00:01:20.374 --> 00:01:27.048
3. Some incidents must reach regulators, funders or insurers within set times.

12
00:01:27.448 --> 00:01:28.048
What you will set up

13
00:01:28.048 --> 00:01:32.241
1. Visible, simple routes from your first activity.

14
00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:37.174
2. Timescales for answering, and a route to someone independent.

15
00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:43.478
3. A list of external reporting duties, confirmed with qualified advice.

16
00:01:43.878 --> 00:01:44.478
What to avoid

17
00:01:44.478 --> 00:01:50.152
Every route leading back to the same one or two founders.

18
00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:54.715
Punishing or ignoring people who raise concerns honestly.

19
00:01:54.715 --> 00:02:01.019
Hiding the routes where participants and volunteers cannot find them.

20
00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:03.419
You design your reporting channels and timescales before you launch.

21
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:07.419
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:12.019
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
